        "original_id": "9ac14a50-c55d-5689-b0be-965b2a986897",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Trax Colton, Louis A. Morelli\n- Companies: 20th Century Fox, 21st Century Fox\n- Roles: motion picture actor, contract player\n- Places: Century City, Los Angeles, Beverly Hills\n- Topics: American film studios, Big Six\n\nFacts:\n- Trax Colton, born Louis A. Morelli on May 26, 1929, is an American former motion picture actor.\n- Between 1960 and 1962, Trax Colton appeared in two films as a contract player for 20th Century Fox.\n- Twentieth Century Fox Film Corporation used the hyphenated name Twentieth Century-Fox Film Corporation from 1935 until 1985.\n- 20th Century Fox is an American film studio currently owned by 21st Century Fox.\n- 20th Century Fox is one of the Big Six major American film studios.\n- 20th Century Fox is located in the Century City area of Los Angeles, just west of Beverly Hills.",
